 "screens_run": 41,
 "notes": "31 daily pre-checks on NIFTY+INDVIX 2012-2020 (points, next-open fills, 3 pts cost) and 10 engine screens 2021-2024. Pre-check: VIX spike-and-turn (VIX pr252>=80 turning) positive but only ~3-4 trades/yr and failed in the engine 2021-24 (11 trades, -25k). VIX/HV>1.5 cross (hold 10d) +4359 pts but 2/3 from 2020; nearby thresholds (1.25) lose -> fragile. Simple vol-timing (long while VIX<EMA10) = just drift (excess +184). Squeeze release long had excess +944 pts on only 16 trades / 9 yrs, 5 trades in the engine -> too rare. Squeeze release short and complacency short (low VIX, VIX lifting, price above EMA20) lose or ~0: short side doesn't work in this family. The 3-of-4 'fear priced but calming' vote is the only rule that held: positive in 8/9 pre-check years, all 7 neighbour variants positive, and positive in every training half 2021H2-2024H2 (no signals in 2021H1 because VIX was low vs the 2020 year). Its weakness is frequency: 27 trades over 2021-24 (below the ~60 the lead asked for), t 1.87. Intraday: ORB(09:15-09:30) futures with the new intraday 15m ATR2 trailing underlying stop: ungated 939 trades -33k; gated VIX pr>=70 +52k / t 0.72 (all from 2024H1), VIX pr<30 +35k / t 0.49 -> no vol-state ORB edge. Suggested gate (vol model == 1) was tried once and is worse than ungated (+215k vs +256k): the vote already selects volatile states; submit ungated.",
 "platform_issues": [
  "No k-of-n vote operator: 3-of-4 votes must be written as any-of(all-of combinations), 4 combos for entry and 4 for exit; a {'votes': [...], 'min': k} group would be cleaner.",
  "highest/lowest default source is high/low; for a VIX close series pass source='close' explicitly (easy to miss)."
 ],
