   "name": "VIX fear-calming vote long (3 of 4), NIFTY futures swing",
   "family": "vol-state",
   "instrument": "futures",
   "hypothesis": "When implied vol is elevated (VIX in its top 30% of the past year, and VIX > 1.3x realised 20d vol) but has started to come off its 5-day high, and NIFTY is below its EMA20, the market is pricing more fear than is being realised; buying futures earns the volatility/risk premium as fear unwinds.",
   "mechanism": "Volatility mean-reverts and VIX-falling-from-high states coincide with short-covering and hedge unwinds; a vote of 4 independent-ish conditions (level, turn, implied-vs-realised spread, price dip) is more stable than one tuned threshold. Exit when <=1 vote remains (fear normalised), after 15 days, or at a 3x daily-ATR stop.",
   "failure_modes": "A real bear market where VIX stays high and the turn is a pause (2018 lost -948 pts in the pre-check, Oct 2008 style). Few trades (~7/yr), so the test can fail on t even if the edge is real. Long-only: rides NIFTY drift partly (but excess vs drift was positive in both the pre-check and training). 2024 carries a large share of rupees because of the 75 lot size from Nov 2024; compare points.",
   "regimes_expected": [
    4,
